Subject: [PATCH] DIAGNOSTIC ONLY: smsc911x: enable the driver's own WARN/TRACE

Upstream hardcodes `#define USE_DEBUG 0` in smsc911x.h, which compiles every
SMSC_WARN()/SMSC_TRACE() down to no_printk(). On the MPS3 Linux harness shell
that made eth0 bring-up completely silent: no PHY/MDIO message ever reached the
console, so we could not tell whether smsc911x_open() was failing loudly or not
reaching those paths at all.

Raise it to 2 so netif_warn()/netif_info() are emitted (still gated at runtime
by the `debug` msg_enable module parameter, so boot with smsc911x.debug=16).

DIAGNOSTIC ONLY -- drop this patch once eth0 bring-up is understood; it is not
intended for the production image.

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/smsc/smsc911x.h
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/smsc/smsc911x.h
@@ -26,7 +26,7 @@
 
 #define TX_FIFO_LOW_THRESHOLD	((u32)1600)
 #define SMSC911X_EEPROM_SIZE	((u32)128)
-#define USE_DEBUG		0
+#define USE_DEBUG		2
 
 /* This is the maximum number of packets to be received every
  * NAPI poll */
